      "content": "The math behind the Fourier Transform is indeed algebraic and involves manipulating the signal's discrete time-domain representation. The frequency domain representation (using sines and cosines) is a consequence of the sleight-of-hand involved in Fourier Transforms. Think of the integral as a weighted sum, where the weights are determined by the signal's amplitude at specific frequencies. The formula helps to isolate the coefficient that weights the amplitude of the sine/cosine function, effectively \" extracting\" the frequency information from the signal.",
